course: dictionary
lesson: 14884
title: Giving back with reciprocate
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: To reciprocate means to give back the same kind of thing that someone gave you. If a friend shares a biscuit with you, you can reciprocate by sharing one of yours. «Mia helped me with my maths, so I helped her with her spelling.» Mia gave help, and I reciprocated by giving help back.
explain: The word can also be about feelings. «Sam liked Priya, but she did not reciprocate his feelings.» Sam felt something kind towards Priya, but she did not feel the same way back. The clue is did not: something was missing from the reply.
explain: Formal writing uses reciprocate for invitations and favours. «The Hendersons invited us to dinner, so we reciprocated with an invitation of our own.» The clue is so: the first invitation came first, and the reply matches it. When you meet reciprocate, ask yourself: what came first, and what came back?
fact: Reciprocate is a verb: I reciprocate, she reciprocates, they reciprocated.
fact: «Reciprocate» means giving back the same kind of thing: a favour for a favour, or a smile for a smile.
fact: «Reciprocate» can also mean returning a feeling, such as liking or love.
fact: «Did not reciprocate» means the other person did not give the same thing back.
fact: Reciprocate is a formal word, often used in stories about friendship, manners and fairness, and in lessons about give and take.
exercise: «The Patels invited us for lunch, so we decided to reciprocate with an invitation to our house.» What does reciprocate mean here? | *To give back an invitation in return | To cook lunch for the whole street | To ask for money | To refuse the lunch politely
exercise: «Tom smiled at Ruby, but she did not reciprocate.» What does did not reciprocate mean? | She ran off to find Tom | She went to sleep | *She did not give the same feeling or kindness back | She smiled even more
exercise: Which word means the same as reciprocate when you return a kind feeling? | Hide | Forget | Ignore | *Return
test: «When Grandma helped me with my knitting, I wanted to reciprocate by baking her a cake.» What does reciprocate mean here? | *To give back a kind act in return | To copy her knitting | To ask for more help | To ignore her help
test: Which sentence uses reciprocate correctly? | Anna reciprocated the bus to school | *Jake helped me carry my bags, so I reciprocated by helping him with his homework | The sun reciprocated the rain | The dog reciprocated by sleeping all day
exam: «Leo lent Ben his pen, and Ben reciprocated the next day.» What does reciprocated mean? | Asked for more pens | *Gave the same kind of favour back | Lost the pen | Refused to help
